Recommends: ffmpeg
Description: real-time ZX Spectrum Next emulator with an integrated debugger
 JNEXT is a real-time, cross-platform ZX Spectrum Next emulator written in
 C++17, based on the official VHDL sources for the ZX Spectrum Next FPGA
 core. It targets developers writing Next software: a debugger showing
 CPU, memory, video layers, sprites, audio and NextREG state live, with
 breakpoints, watches and step-backward execution, plus a headless mode
 for running programs under CI.
